From: Domenico D'Arrigo <d.darrigo@outlook.it>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 19:40:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 202/204] security/tpm: Firmware version into PCR 1 outside
 ChromeOS

vboot extends the firmware version into PCR_FW_VER, which has no prompt
and is 10 on every board. PCR 10 is where ChromeOS keeps it, but on
other systems it is the PCR of the OS: Linux IMA extends its measurement
list there, starting with boot_aggregate, and a replay of that list
assumes the PCR was zero when the kernel started. With vboot's extend in
it the IMA log no longer matches the PCR.

Outside ChromeOS, put it in PCR 1 with vboot's boot mode and HWID
(PCR_BOOT_MODE and PCR_HWID are 1 there too), the PCR of the platform
configuration in the TCG PC Client profile.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/security/tpm/Kconfig | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/security/tpm/Kconfig b/src/security/tpm/Kconfig
index c1d6797d3d..0e602bec15 100644
--- a/src/security/tpm/Kconfig
+++ b/src/security/tpm/Kconfig
@@ -173,7 +173,8 @@ config PCR_SRTM
 
 config PCR_FW_VER
 	int
-	default 10
+	default 10 if CHROMEOS
+	default 1
 
 # PCR for measuring data which changes during runtime
 # e.g. CMOS, NVRAM...
